INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S LOG ROOM - NIGHT

Cramped. A circular desk. Ship's barometer, brass lamp, rows of leather-bound logbooks. Fog presses on the window. The foghorn sounds every ninety seconds.

INSPECTOR GWENDOLYN ADEBAYO-HARTWELL, 50s, oilskin coat dripping on the planks, sits at the desk with a lamp and a stack of logbooks. She flips pages with a gloved hand, jots notes in a pocket pad, taps a pen against her teeth. The foghorn sounds. She does not flinch.

GWENDOLYN
(to the room)
October ninth. "Light functioning. Visibility poor." October tenth. "Light functioning. Visibility poor." October eleventh.

She stops. Runs a finger over the ink.

GWENDOLYN (CONT'D)
"Light functioning. Visibility poor. Mr. Pellew did not return."

She flips back. Forward. Back again.

GWENDOLYN (CONT'D)
Three entries, same handwriting. Same ink. Same hour. But the first two were written by a man who is alive, and the third by a man who isn't.

She lifts the lamp and holds the page to the flame. Behind the ink, faint, a second line shows through, written in a different hand and scratched out.

GWENDOLYN (CONT'D)
(reading, softly)
"He did not fall."

Her radio crackles on the desk. She snatches it up.

HARBORMASTER (V.O.)
(over the radio)
Inspector? You got anything yet?

GWENDOLYN
I have a log that lies, Harbormaster. And a keeper who's missing.

HARBORMASTER (V.O.)
Pellew's boat washed up on the rocks. Empty.

GWENDOLYN
Was the lamp lit?

HARBORMASTER (V.O.)
Aye. All night.

GWENDOLYN
Who lit it?

HARBORMASTER (V.O.)
You tell me, Inspector. You're the one in the tower.

She sets the radio down. The foghorn sounds. A floorboard above her creaks. She looks at the ceiling, at the spiral stair, and then at the pen in her hand.

She rises, slips the log into her coat, and climbs.
